---
import { formatInt, formatMegabytes, formatMs, formatPercent } from "../lib/format";
import { nanosecondsToMs } from "../lib/metrics";
import { browser, routing, validation } from "../lib/reports";
import Spread from "./Spread.astro";

const wakeUp = formatMs(nanosecondsToMs(routing.cold_initialization_nanoseconds), 0);
const matrix = validation.pooled_matrix;
const pooledPrecision = matrix.true_positive / (matrix.true_positive + matrix.false_positive);
const pooledRecall = matrix.true_positive / (matrix.true_positive + matrix.false_negative);
const cleanRows = matrix.false_positive + matrix.true_negative;
const cleanWarned = matrix.false_positive / cleanRows;
const startingSize = formatMegabytes(browser.browser_builds.explicit_only.brotli_total_bytes, 1);
---
<Spread id="credo" label="the credo">
  <div class="page l">
    <svg class="emblem" viewBox="0 0 80 96" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sacredHeart"></use></svg>
    <p class="rubric">the credo</p>
    <h2 id="credo-title" class="title">A free internet can still be a safe one</h2>
    <p class="creed">We believe the web should stay free, private, and safe at the same time, and that no one should have to trade one for another.</p>
    <p class="copy">The serious profanity and toxicity checks today are neural models. Models want gigabytes of memory and a machine you do not own, so the text goes to a server, and the safety of a conversation becomes someone else's log line.</p>
    <p class="copy">A message can be caught before any of that happens. On the keyboard. In the tab it was written in. For {startingSize}.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="page r">
    <div class="antiphon">
      <p class="not">Not a moderation pipeline.</p>
      <p class="but">A nudge before send.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="copy">blasphem exists to stop a hostile message from leaving, in the second the writer can still change it. It does not rank a feed, it does not ban an account, and it does not decide what is true. Those are jobs for a system that can see a whole community. This one sees one draft, and only while it is being written.</p>
    <p class="copy">That narrow scope buys the whole design. No model means fixed integer tables. Fixed tables mean a small download, a {wakeUp} wake-up, and a verdict in under a millisecond for a short message. Nothing is sent, so nothing can leak.</p>
    <p class="copy">It also sets the price, and we pay it openly: <b>we trade recall for precision</b>. When blasphem warns, it is right {formatPercent(pooledPrecision, 1)} of the time, and it warns on {formatPercent(cleanWarned, 1)} of the {formatInt(cleanRows)} clean validation messages. It also misses. Pooled recall is {formatPercent(pooledRecall, 0)}, and per language it runs from single digits to the high eighties.</p>
    <p class="copy">A pre-send nudge that cries wolf gets dismissed, and then it catches nothing at all. One that stays quiet until it is sure keeps its one chance to be heard. Read <a href="#reckoning">the reckoning</a> for every number behind that trade.</p>
  </div>
</Spread>

<style>
  .page.l {
    position: relative;
  }
  .emblem {
    position: absolute;
    right: 8%;
    top: 64px;
    width: 260px;
    height: 312px;
    color: var(--blood);
    opacity: 0.1;
    z-index: -1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .creed {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    max-width: 24ch;
    font-family: var(--font-goth);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--blood-ink);
  }
  .antiphon {
    margin: 0 0 26px;
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--blood-hair);
  }
  .not,
  .but {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-goth);
    font-size: clamp(22px, 1.9vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .not {
    color: var(--taupe-ink);
    text-decoration: line-through;
    text-decoration-color: var(--blood-hair);
  }
  .but {
    color: var(--bone);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .emblem {
      width: 160px;
      height: 192px;
      right: 0;
      top: 40px;
    }
  }
</style>
